(PRC-41 — undocumented precision: an argument list containing anything
 that is not text makes the exec FAIL and set the error flag, in both the
 literal and the list-variable form. Nothing crashes and the program keeps
 running, so memory safety holds; the manual just never says the elements
 have to be text, and its phrase "regardless of the list's contents"
 (LANGUAGE.md:4179-4180) reads as though any contents are handled.
 Minimal repro at D3.vox.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-41.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   a literal list with a number in it failed the exec
   a list variable with mixed types failed the exec
   alpha beta
)
Execute "/bin/echo" with arguments [42, "beta"].
On error print "a literal list with a number in it failed the exec".
a list called 'the mixed arguments' is ["alpha", 42, true, 3.5].
Execute "/bin/echo" with arguments 'the mixed arguments'.
On error print "a list variable with mixed types failed the exec".
a list called 'the text arguments' is ["alpha", "beta"].
Execute "/bin/echo" with arguments 'the text arguments'.
On error print "the all-text control failed too".
